--- C0/C1 the Chae+21 environmental eta distribution (n = 109) ---
  [maxclu] eta >= 0.30:   0 | eta >= 0.10:   0 | eta >= 0.03:   0 | max eta = 0.0182 | median = 0.00501
  [noclu] eta >= 0.30:   0 | eta >= 0.10:   0 | eta >= 0.03:   0 | max eta = 0.0022 | median = 0.00061
  [repo estimator cross-check, n = 175] max eta = 0.0388, count eta >= 0.3 = 0
  [PASS] C0 the work order's premise '30-40 galaxies at eta >= 0.3' is FALSE on the archival record: the Chae+21 environmental table has ZERO galaxies at eta >= 0.3 (maxclu 0, noclu 0); the repo's own reconstruction agrees (max eta = 0.0388) -- the SPARC-environmental channel CANNOT carry the direction test at the amplitudes the plan assumes
  [PASS] C1 the strongest environmental field on record is eta = 0.0388 -- two orders of magnitude below the plan's 0.3 threshold

--- C2 the regime: does any SPARC curve even ENTER the EFE zone? ---
  SPARC curves read: 175; R_out/r_EFE computed on 218 matched galaxies (both footings counted separately)
  median R_out/r_EFE = 0.256; galaxies reaching the EFE zone (R_out >= r_EFE): 15/218
  [PASS] C2 the regime, computed on SPARC: median R_out/r_EFE = 0.256 < 1 and only 15/218 curves reach the EFE-dominated zone -- the direction test is UNDERPOWERED-BY-CONSTRUCTION on the environmental channel (h28's WALLABY finding, reproduced here on SPARC)

